Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:45:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 374/405] Part: Shape.tessellate(tolerance, normals=True) gives
 a normal for each point

The normals out of the solid, from OCC's triangulation; the points are
not shared between faces so that edges stay sharp. A room's smooth
shading asked them point by point from Python (Surface.parameter,
normalAt): more than ten minutes at 1 mm (reported on 0.7.9).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
